{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And the thing does not come to pass.</b> For indeed a commandment is not newly instituted even temporarily for the multitude, unless it is accompanied by some sign — as it was with Joshua in the splitting of the Jordan and the fall of the wall of Jericho (Joshua 3:6), and with Elijah in the descent of fire from heaven (I Kings 18:38). Indeed, the command of the prophet who said אֶל רֵעֵהוּ הַכֵּנִי נָא (I Kings 20:35) was directed to his fellow prophet like himself, who knew that it was the word of HaShem; therefore he was punished when he refused."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The Sforno cites Joshua 3:6 for both the Jordan splitting and Jericho's wall; the wall's fall is narrated in Joshua 6, but I have kept his citation exactly as he gives it."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:21:46.991639255Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}